Your mule is not yet here.	你的騾子尚未到此。
My pleasure, m'lord.	樂意效勞，吾王。
Beggin' your pardon, m'lord?	恕小人失禮，吾王？
The skies are clear.  'Tis a good day to begin your search.	天色晴朗。正是啟程尋覓的好日子。
Considering how much of Camelot is made of this grey stone, there must have been a great deal of it around at one time.	肯萊特有大半是以這種灰石建成，想當年此地想必蘊藏甚豐。
The inner courtyard is guarded by your loyal men.	內庭由你忠誠的士兵把守。
Your warhorse and a pack mule have been prepared for your journey.	你的戰馬與一頭馱運的騾子，都已為此行備妥。
It does not look happy about being chosen for this mission, nor about carrying your pack of provisions.	牠似乎不太樂意被選中執行此行，也不情願馱著你的補給包。
Your mule is being prepared for the journey.	你的騾子正為此行做準備。
Aye, those are stairs.	正是，那是階梯。
I can sense the mingling of pride and despair that fills you as you look upon your stronghold and home.	我能感受到，你望著這座要塞與家園時，心中驕傲與絕望交織。
The thick, stone walls make Camelot virtually impregnable against normal attack.	厚重的石牆使肯萊特幾乎無懈可擊，尋常攻勢難以攻破。
Against this curse of plague and drought, however, the thickest of stone walls is no defense.	然而面對這場瘟疫與乾旱的詛咒，再厚的石牆也無濟於事。
It is the main entrance to your castle proper.	這是通往城堡本體的正門。
The window in the tower is a lookout.	塔上的窗口是瞭望口。
This tunnel leads to the portcullis which is your outside gate.	這條甬道通往閘門，也就是你的外門。
It is part of the defensive system of Camelot.	這是肯萊特防禦體系的一部分。
Your horse is a sturdy and well-trained stallion, bred to be steady in danger and battle.	你的坐騎是一匹強健且訓練有素的公馬，育種便是為了臨危與臨陣皆能沉穩不亂。
Your grooms prepare the horse and pack mule.  When you are ready, they will be here.	馬伕正在備妥坐騎與馱運的騾子。待你準備就緒，牠們便會在此候命。
You should know your horse better than that, Arthur. He is a stallion.	你該比這更了解自己的坐騎才是，亞瑟。牠是匹公馬。
Your guards bear the Royal shields of Camelot.	你的衛兵持著肯萊特的皇家盾牌。
Your own shield is familiar to you. Your guards, of course, bear the Royal shields of Camelot.	你對自己的盾牌再熟悉不過。至於你的衛兵，自然持著肯萊特的皇家盾牌。
Your guards have little need for their lances these days.	你的衛兵近來已鮮少用得上長槍。
It contains water, food, blankets, extra clothing and such things as you may want on a long journey.	裡頭裝著水、糧食、毛毯、備用衣物，以及長途旅程中你可能用得上的物件。
Your servants are preparing a pack for your trip. It will be ready to go when you are.	你的僕從正為此行備妥行囊，待你準備完畢，行囊也將備妥待發。
Your own special tack has been used.	你專屬的馬具已然備上。
There is no tack here.	此處並無馬具。
Galahad is well liked amongst the guards.  They would be most likely to have news of him.	葛拉漢在衛兵之間頗受愛戴，他們最有可能得知他的消息。
A clumsy weapon for a long trip. Excaliber is the best weapon you could want.	長途跋涉帶這種笨重武器不甚妥當。聖劍才是你能擁有的最佳武器。
There will be time enough for that on the journey.	此事路上自有時間再說。
What the devil for?  Have you lost all common sense?	這究竟是為了什麼？你莫非失了常識？
There is no pack here.	此處並無行囊。
Your horse is already here.	你的坐騎已在此處。
Your mule is already here.	你的騾子已在此處。
It is being prepared. When your own preparations are complete, it will surely be ready and waiting for you.	牠正在備妥中。待你自己準備就緒，牠必已備妥候著你。
It is not only difficult, but pointless.	此事不僅困難，更是毫無意義。
Lead and it will follow.	你只管引路，牠自會跟上。
Your grooms have seen to such details, though you are wise to think of it.	這類細節馬伕早已辦妥，不過你想到這一點也算明智。
A horse is for riding.	馬是用來騎的。
Why would you want to ride a bony little mule when you have your fine stallion?	你既有這匹駿馬，何苦去騎那頭瘦骨嶙峋的小騾子？
Nay, 'tis the other way around. The mule follows you.	不，恰恰相反。是騾子跟著你走。
Why do you draw your sword here?  You are safely surrounded by your own men.	你為何在此拔劍？你身邊盡是自己的士兵，安全無虞。
This is no time for sword practice with your men.	此刻不是與士兵練劍的時候。
The legend says that a man with violence in his soul will be destroyed if he touches the Grail.	傳說中，心懷暴戾之人若觸碰聖杯，必遭毀滅。
It is a rather ordinary shield.	這是面相當普通的盾牌。
It is a rather ordinary spear.	這是柄相當普通的長矛。
Forgive me, sire, I do not understand.	恕臣不解，陛下。
Standing closer to a guard would help.	靠近某位衛兵些，或許有幫助。
You are my king, sire.	你是臣的君王，陛下。
I am your faithful and loyal servant, my liege.	臣是陛下忠誠效命的僕從，吾主。
Your horse, mule and pack are being prepared.	你的坐騎、騾子與行囊都在備妥中。
Your horse is saddled and ready. The mule bears your pack of provisions.	你的坐騎已備鞍待發，騾子則馱著你的補給行囊。
I have no news of him, m'lord.	小人並無他的消息，吾王。
She should be in the castle, m'lord.	她應當在城堡裡，吾王。
I am sure you know more than me about that, sire, me being only a guard and all.	陛下想必比小人更清楚此事，畢竟小人不過是個衛兵。
The man yonder, to the left of the arch, is the smartest of all of us, m'lord.	拱門左側那人，是我們當中最機靈的一個，吾王。
May God protect you, m'lord.	願上帝保佑你，吾王。
May God lead you to the Grail, my King.	願上帝引領你尋得聖杯，吾王。
We pray for your success, King Arthur.	我們為你的成功祈禱，亞瑟王。
Mithras guide and protect you.	願米夏拉引導並庇佑你。
Such miserliness does not become a king.	如此吝嗇，實非人君之風。
All the armour gets in the way, fortunately.	所幸這身甲冑正好擋路，礙手礙腳。
They have no use for it.	他們用不著這個。
Very sweet of you, m'lord.	你真是體貼，吾王。
You don't have any money.	你身上沒有錢。
Bless you, m'lord!	願神保佑你，吾王！
Thank'ee most kindly, m'lord!	多謝吾王厚賜！
Praise be your generosity, King Arthur!	讚頌你的慷慨，亞瑟王！
Arthur, will you please stop trying to give away your most valuable possessions.	亞瑟，別再想著把你最貴重的物件送人了。
As you command.	遵命。
Their weapons are inferior to Excaliber.	他們的武器比不上聖劍。
Besides which, they need them to defend Camelot in your absence.	何況你不在時，他們還得靠這些武器防守肯萊特。
You guard needs it.	你的衛兵需要它。
They are unable to do that.	他們辦不到此事。
Their place is here, guarding Camelot.	他們的崗位在此，守衛肯萊特。
Is this some odd Celtic word, m'lord?	這是什麼古怪的凱爾特語嗎，吾王？
Greetings, my liege.	向吾主問安。
Uh....no, thank you, m'lord.	呃……不了，多謝，吾王。
What a thoroughly disgusting idea.	好個令人作嘔的念頭。
These are not the thoughts of a pure man.	這可不是清白之人該有的念頭。
The Christians say that stealing is a sin and no sinner may lay hands upon the Grail and live.	基督徒說偷竊是一種罪，罪人若碰觸聖杯，必難逃一死。
You can only help us by bringing back the Grail before it is too late.	你唯有趁一切還來得及，將聖杯尋回，才能真正幫上我們。
Your horse is trained only to fight your enemies, not your friends.	你的坐騎只受過與敵人交戰的訓練，不會對付你的朋友。
You're not on the horse.	你並未騎在馬上。
That is not becoming of a king.	此舉有失人君之儀。
His horse was sent back to our care by the Harbourmaster of Southampton.	南安普頓港的港務司已將他的坐騎送回，交由我們照料。
Along with a message from the Harbourmaster that Sir Galahad took ship to the Far East.	港務司還捎來口信，說葛拉漢爵士已搭船前往遠東。
Very well, m'lord.	遵命，吾王。
My Lord King, I have news of Galahad, if you would care to hear it.	吾王陛下，臣有葛拉漢的消息，不知陛下是否願聞。
That is all I know, m'lord.  Godspeed you on your mission.	小人所知僅此而已，吾王。願你此行一路平安。
My pleasure, m'lord.  I only thought to mention in case no-one else had told you, sir.	樂意效勞，吾王。小人只是想著，若無人稟報，還是說一聲的好。
Your horse and mule are being prepared for the journey.	你的坐騎與騾子正為此行備妥。
Your horse and mule await you in the courtyard.	你的坐騎與騾子在庭院中候著你。
The skies are clear and the weather holding good. A fine time to begin a journey.	天色晴朗，天候良好，正是啟程的好時機。
Amazingly enough, it is also paved with stone.	說來也是，這裡同樣鋪著石板。
Here your journey begins in earnest. Search your soul and be sure you are ready.	你的旅程將自此正式展開。捫心自問，確認自己已準備就緒。
Once you leave Camelot, I will seal the castle with a powerful spell of protection. You will not be able to re-enter until you have the Grail.	你一旦離開肯萊特，我便會以強大的護城法術封印城堡。在你尋得聖杯之前，你將無法再度進入。
This is the main gate of Camelot.	這是肯萊特的正門。
It stands tall, strong and proud. Yet if you fail, it will not endure.	它高聳、堅固、巍然而立。然而你若失敗，它終將不保。
The top of the tunnel is also stone.	甬道的頂部同樣是石造。
It is fairly dark in here. There is not much to see.	這裡相當昏暗，沒什麼好看的。
It leads to the courtyard and the main door to the castle.	它通往庭院與城堡的正門。
The boulders are part of the castle's foundation.	這些巨石是城堡地基的一部分。
This heavy portcullis was built to withstand even a battering ram.	這座沉重的閘門，就連攻城槌也難以撼動。
You surely know your own symbol, Arthur, the red dragon of Pendragon.	你當然認得自己的家徽，亞瑟，那是潘德拉貢的紅龍。
The walls are massive and built of stone.	城牆雄偉厚重，以石砌成。
Travel on and the map will guide you.	繼續前行，地圖自會為你指路。
There is no moat. Your protection is in the high walls and steep cliffs.	這裡沒有護城河，你的屏障在於高聳的城牆與陡峭的懸崖。
Camelot was designed without a drawbridge.	肯萊特建造之初便未設吊橋。
He is safe within. Worry not.	他在裡頭很安全，無須擔憂。
And fall to your death? Ridiculous.	摔下去送命？荒唐。
You already are on your horse.	你已騎在馬上。
You don't need to get off your horse.	你不必下馬。
It IS open.	它確實是開著的。
You may not return, Arthur, until you have found the Grail...or died in trying. To turn aside or abandon your sacred mission means the certain death of all you hold dear.	亞瑟，除非你尋得聖杯……或死於途中，否則你不得回返。若你轉身逃避或放棄這項神聖使命，你所珍愛的一切必將盡數殞落。
You can hardly begin a long and arduous journey in your court clothes.	你穿著宮廷袍服，如何踏上這般漫長艱辛的旅途。
Do you think this is a fairytale where you can simply run off without preparation?	你以為這是童話故事，可以毫無準備便說走就走？
Certainly.  As soon as you have a horse under you, as common sense would require.	當然可以，只消你胯下有匹馬便行，這是常理所需。
This is no time for petulance or foolishness.   The lives of all your people hang in the balance.	此刻不是任性胡鬧的時候。你全體子民的性命，皆懸於一線。
It IS lowered	它確實已經放下。
It will be done.  You need not worry.	此事必會辦妥，你無須擔憂。
Excaliber is a powerful sword, but even it cannot break this portcullis.	聖劍雖是把威力強大的劍，卻也劈不開這座閘門。
There is no need.  It will follow.	無此必要，牠自會跟上。
It is on the mule which follows you.	它就在跟著你的那頭騾子身上。
It is rather early for that.  You have not even begun to travel.	現在說這個還太早，你連旅程都還沒展開。
If it is ready, it will be in the courtyard.	若已備妥，便會在庭院裡。
What an utterly ridiculous idea.	好個荒唐透頂的念頭。
They are at their posts where they belong.	他們都在自己該駐守的崗位上。
This is your mission alone, Arthur.  They cannot help you.	這是你獨自的使命，亞瑟，他們幫不上忙。
It is terribly unwise to start a sacred mission without the blessings of the gods.	未得諸神庇佑便展開這神聖的使命，實在極不明智。
